<title>AUSTRIA: IRAN SAYS OPEC SOLVES ISSUE OF QUOTA COMPLIANCE.</title>
<headline>IRAN SAYS OPEC SOLVES ISSUE OF QUOTA COMPLIANCE.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iranian oil minister Gholamreza Aghazadeh said on Wednesday that OPEC ministers had solved the issue of quota compliance.</p>
<p>Venezuela's Erwin Arrieta said that the ministers would meet again at 0800 GMT on Thursday at the Secretariat.  </p>
<p>Aghazadeh and Arrieta were speaking at the end of a closed session of all OPEC delegation heads in the hotel suite of the OPEC President Abdullah Salem al-Badri, the Libyan minister.</p>
<p>Badri was expected to give a news briefing shortly.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
